<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pinsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pinsk is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brest-france">Brest</a> region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, where the Pina joins the Pripyat, in the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pripet-marshes">Pinsk Marshes</a>. First recorded in 1097, it was a town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turov">Turov</a> lands and later a Lithuanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> duchy. In modern times it had a large Jewish community, most of whom were murdered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pinsk.jpg" alt="Pinsk" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Liilia Moroz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pinsk_Lenina_street.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
